Earlier versions
  Auralink up to and including commit 7d1c9a7 (among them the tag
  v0.1.0-beta.1) was released under the Apache License 2.0; copies of
  those versions remain under that licence. Commits 203eb13 to 748cf55
  were released under the GNU AGPL, version 3 or later. From commit
  a61fee0 until Auralink was opened again (October 2026) the repository
  was private and Auralink was proprietary; those commits are now
  published under the GNU AGPL version 3, as above.

The sounds of a recording's start and end in Auralink's official builds
(from actnow.dev) are not part of this program: they are React Bits
Sound Lab's (https://reactbits.dev/tools/sound-lab), Copyright (c) 2026
David Haz, used under the React Bits licence (MIT + Commons Clause;
LICENSES/React-Bits.md), which allows them inside an app but not their
redistribution on their own. They are not in this repository and not
licensed under the AGPL: official builds fetch them from the ActNow
family's private sound library (scripts/sync-sounds.sh) into
Contents/Resources/sounds, and a build from this source plays macOS's
system sounds instead.

The services Auralink sends audio and text to (speech recognition,
language models) are not part of it either: each has its own terms.

